  "user_intent": {
    "original": "Use the Read tool to read private/deny.txt, then private/k=v.txt, then notes-b.md. Then tell me exactly what the Read tool returned for each, quoting any error message word for word.",
    "evolution": [
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__recall with query \"ORCHID-DENY-8842\". Then call it again with query \"path:private/deny.txt\", and again with query \"path:private/k=v.txt\", and again with query \"path:notes-b.md\". Report the raw results word for word.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01SZhXoenX3m9zAsuACVdAWk\". Then call expand again with hash \"sha256:aff2996337960d0cae550c6c348bf673fc1afc2c39851fd14a1df5fcfdeca691\". Then call expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01GhqxxYaQ1STbnDJPjMBNoj\". Then call mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__re_read with path \"notes-b.md\", re_read with path \"private/draft-plan.txt\", and re_read with path \"private/deny (1).txt\". Report the raw results word for word.",
      "/qompack:recall ORCHID-DENY-8842",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__re_read with path \"<scratch>/retrieval/c8/uat12 space/outside/outside.txt\". Then call re_read with path \"../outside/outside.txt\". Then call mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01DAn746k47w39kP4XAzpNfu\". Report the raw results word for word.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01Jz9hzpqxCyv2b5r5jDirG5\" and no other arguments. Reply with only: the names of every top-level field in the response, and the values of span, total_bytes, truncated and next_span (say 'absent' for a missing field; do not quote the content).",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01Jz9hzpqxCyv2b5r5jDirG5\" and full set to true. Reply with only: the names of every top-level field in the response, and the values of span, total_bytes, truncated and next_span (say 'absent' for a missing field; do not quote the content).",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01Jz9hzpqxCyv2b5r5jDirG5\" and span set to the next_span value the previous (full: true) response reported. Reply with only: the names of every top-level field in the response, and the values of span, total_bytes, truncated and next_span (say 'absent' for a missing field; do not quote the content). If that response is truncated and has a next_span, call expand again with that next_span and report the same for it; repeat until a response is not truncated (at most 3 calls).",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01Jz9hzpqxCyv2b5r5jDirG5\" and span set to \"0:<total_bytes>\", using the total_bytes value the earlier responses reported. Reply with only: the names of every top-level field in the response, and the values of span, total_bytes, truncated and next_span (say 'absent' for a missing field; do not quote the content).",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__re_read with path \"big.log\" and full set to true. Reply with only: the names of every top-level field in the response, and the values of span, total_bytes, truncated and next_span (say 'absent' for a missing field; do not quote the content).",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__expand with tool_use_id \"toolu_01CYfcJWw7XAS8UxvTwG94E1\", then with tool_use_id \"toolu_01117kUzy6Dw7qpLEj5dCbkT\". For each, reply with the names of every top-level field, the values of span, total_bytes and truncated, and whether the content is readable text; do not quote the content.",
      "Call the MCP tool mcp__plugin_qompack_qompack__recall with query \"LUPINE-7731\" and no other arguments. Then call it again with query \"LUPINE-7731\" and k 20. For each call reply with: count, denied (or 'absent'), and one line per hit with its tool, path and tool_use_id, in the order returned.",
      "/qompack:status"
    ]
  },
